t-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"content-text\">\n          <p class=\"instrument-text\">By imaging the surfaces of Vesta and Ceres, the framing cameras will enable scientists to map the topography, albedo and color, and to determine their shapes, volumes, and spin rates.</p>\n          <div class=\"person-block\">\n            <div class=\"person-photo\">\n              <span style=\"color:#888;font-size:10px;\">[Photo: Holger Sierks]</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"person-name\">Holger Sierks</div>\n            <div class=\"person-role\">Framing Camera Lead, MPS</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content-image\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder\">[Image: Framing Camera instrument]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Center: Asteroid & Spacecraft -->\n    <div class=\"center-area\">\n      <div class=\"center-image\">\n        <div class=\"orbit-ring\"></div>\n        <div class=\"asteroid-shape\"></div>\n        <div class=\"beam\"></div>\n        <div class=\"beam2\"></div>\n        <div style=\"position:absolute;top:50px;right:60px;width:70px;height:30px;background:#555;border-radius:2px;\">\n          <div style=\"position:absolute;left:-20px;top:5px;width:20px;height:20px;background:#3366aa;\"></div>\n          <div style=\"position:absolute;right:-20px;top:5px;width:20px;height:20px;background:#3366aa;\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Top Right: Gravity Science -->\n    <div class=\"instrument-section top-right\">\n      <div class=\"instrument-title\">\n        Gravity Science\n        <span class=\"flag flag-us\"></span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"content-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"content-text\">\n          <p class=\"instrument-text\">Gravity science: the spacecraft transmits a radio signal to Earth through its high gain antenna that changes in frequency as the spacecraft's speed changes when flying over areas of different densities. The collective set of information on the mass variations or concentrations is called the gravitational field of the body/planet.</p>\n          <div class=\"person-block\">\n            <div class=\"person-photo\">\n              <span style=\"color:#888;font-size:10px;\">[Photo: Sami Asmar]</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"person-name\">Sami Asmar</div>\n            <div class=\"person-role\">Gravity Science Lead, JPL</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content-image\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder\">[Image: High gain antenna / spacecraft]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Bottom Left: GRaND -->\n    <div class=\"instrument-section bottom-left\">\n      <div class=\"instrument-title\">\n        Gamma Ray Neutron Detector\n        <span class=\"flag flag-us\"></span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"content-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"content-text\">\n          <p class=\"instrument-text\">GRaND measures elemental abundances on the surfaces of Vesta and Ceres, offering insight into their respective formation and evolution</p>\n          <div class=\"person-block\">\n            <div class=\"person-photo\">\n              <span style=\"color:#888;font-size:10px;\">[Photo: Tom Prettyman]</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"person-name\">Tom Prettyman</div>\n            <div class=\"person-role\">GRaND Team Lead, PSI</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content-image\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder\">[Image: GRaND instrument]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Bottom Right: VIR -->\n    <div class=\"instrument-section bottom-right\">\n      <div class=\"instrument-title\">\n        Visible &amp; Infrared Spectrometer\n        <span class=\"flag flag-it\"></span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"content-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"content-text\">\n          <p class=\"instrument-text\">VIR measures reflected sunlight and emitted thermal radiation from the surfaces of the targets. Scientists extract and then map mineralogical signatures and thermal properties. These properties hold clues to the history and formation mechanisms of Vesta and Ceres.</p>\n          <div class=\"person-block\">\n            <div class=\"person-photo\">\n              <span style=\"color:#888;font-size:10px;\">[Photo: Angioletta Coradini]</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"person-name\">Angioletta Coradini</div>\n            <div class=\"person-role\">VIR Team Leader, INAF</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"content-image\">\n          <div class=\"placeholder\">[Image: VIR spectrometer instrument]</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Center Text -->\n    <div class=\"center-text\" style=\"grid-column: 2; grid-row: 2; align-self: center;\">\n      In its journey to the main asteroid belt to orbit two diverse protoplanets, Vesta and Ceres, Dawn is carrying a suite of sophisticated scientific instruments to collect data that will inform us about the early formation of our solar system.\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- URL -->\n    <div class=\"url-section\">\n      <a href=\"http://dawn.jpl.nasa.gov\">http://dawn.jpl.nasa.gov</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>",
